ation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":4,"prompt":"How would you separate legitimate from unresolved and support your conclusion?","anchor":"One address-matched pair are siblings confirmed actively working. Another includes an unconfirmed identity with 14 biweekly paychecks and no timesheet or badge activity on file. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B43-PY-01-ManagerConfirmation-Memo.pdf","options":["One address-matched pair are siblings confirmed actively working. Another includes an unconfirmed identity with 14 biweekly paychecks and no timesheet or badge activity on file.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":5,"prompt":"How would you escalate potential payroll exposure and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Escalate unresolved identity to Internal Audit and HR Security; calculate exposure from 14 paychecks and check whether receiving account is active. Do not assert fraud before investigation. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B43-PY-01-ManagerConfirmation-Memo.pdf","options":["Escalate unresolved identity to Internal Audit and HR Security; calculate exposure from 14 paychecks and check whether receiving account is active. Do not assert fraud before investigation.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0}]'::jsonb);
insert into tib_sweep_private.bank(chapter,questions) values (44,'[{"id":1,"prompt":"How would you establish Basic Pay changes and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Extract the 47 Infotype 0008 Basic Pay changes with old value, new value, changer and timestamp. Preserve scope and change log. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B44-PY-02-BasicPayChangeLog.xlsx","options":["Extract the 47 Infotype 0008 Basic Pay changes with old value, new value, changer and timestamp. Preserve scope and change log.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":2,"prompt":"How would you match independent approvals and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Cross-reference all 47 changes with HR workflow completion evidence. Forty-four show complete independent approval; three lack approval records. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B44-PY-02-ApprovalCrossReference.xlsx","options":["Cross-reference all 47 changes with HR workflow completion evidence. Forty-four show complete independent approval; three lack approval records.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":3,"prompt":"How would you quantify pay impact and support your conclusion?","anchor":"For each of three unapproved changes, calculate the rate difference and affected pay periods. Do not invent a total without payroll data. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B44-PY-02-DollarImpact-Calc.xlsx","options":["For each of three unapproved changes, calculate the rate difference and affected pay periods. Do not invent a total without payroll data.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":4,"prompt":"How would you inspect PFCG role design and support your conclusion?","anchor":"All three unapproved changes were made by one HR administrator whose PFCG role allows both Basic Pay changes and approval. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B44-PY-02-PFCG-RoleReview.pdf","options":["All three unapproved changes were made by one HR administrator whose PFCG role allows both Basic Pay changes and approval.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":5,"prompt":"How would you recommend role separation and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Separate Basic Pay change and approval privileges; check whether other HR administrator roles share the same combination. Document remediation and retest. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B44-PY-02-PFCG-RoleReview.pdf","options":["Separate Basic Pay change and approval privileges; check whether other HR administrator roles share the same combination. Document remediation and retest.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0}]'::jsonb);
insert into tib_sweep_private.bank(chapter,questions) values (45,'[{"id":1,"prompt":"How would you establish off-cycle population and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Obtain the 22 fiscal-quarter off-cycle payroll runs. Record source, period, entity and report parameters; preserve raw export. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B45-PY-03-OffCycleRunPopulation.xlsx","options":["Obtain the 22 fiscal-quarter off-cycle payroll runs. Record source, period, entity and report parameters; preserve raw export.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":2,"prompt":"How would you compare requester and approver and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Review requester and approver identities on all 22 runs. Twenty-one show different people; one bonus correction shows the same person in both roles. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B45-PY-03-RequesterApprover-Comparison.xlsx","options":["Review requester and approver identities on all 22 runs. Twenty-one show different people; one bonus correction shows the same person in both roles.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":3,"prompt":"How would you check payment justifications and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Sample eight runs and compare payment details to HR and Finance supporting records. All eight match within immaterial rounding. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B45-PY-03-JustificationSample.pdf","options":["Sample eight runs and compare payment details to HR and Finance supporting records. All eight match within immaterial rounding.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":4,"prompt":"How would you analyze off-cycle trends and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Compare off-cycle payments as a share of total payroll over the trailing four quarters. The proportion rises from 2.1% to 6.4%. Investigate the cause. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B45-PY-03-TrendAnalysis.xlsx","options":["Compare off-cycle payments as a share of total payroll over the trailing four quarters. The proportion rises from 2.1% to 6.4%. Investigate the cause.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":5,"prompt":"How would you recommend controls and follow-up and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Document the single approval conflict, recommend a second approver above a materiality threshold, and separately investigate whether regular-cycle breakdown, business events or legitimate exceptions explain the rise. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B45-PY-03-TrendAnalysis.xlsx","options":["Document the single approval conflict, recommend a second approver above a materiality threshold, and separately investigate whether regular-cycle breakdown, business events or legitimate exceptions explain the rise.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0}]'::jsonb);
insert into tib_sweep_private.bank(chapter,questions) values (46,'[{"id":1,"prompt":"How would you scope Q3 payroll totals and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Review Q3 payroll posting summary: gross pay $4,182,600; combined deductions and employer costs $1,196,400; net $2,986,200. Preserve source and parameters. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B46-PY-04-PayrollPostingSummary.xlsx","options":["Review Q3 payroll posting summary: gross pay $4,182,600; combined deductions and employer costs $1,196,400; net $2,986,200. Preserve source and parameters.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":2,"prompt":"How would you obtain GL balances and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Use SE16N read-only reporting to obtain GL balances for payroll expense and payroll liability accounts for the same period. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B46-PY-04-GLBalances.xlsx","options":["Use SE16N read-only reporting to obtain GL balances for payroll expense and payroll liability accounts for the same period.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":3,"prompt":"How would you reconcile and quantify and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Gross pay and employer-cost postings reconcile exactly. The payroll liability balance is $38,400 below the payroll-supported amount. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B46-PY-04-Reconciliation.xlsx","options":["Gross pay and employer-cost postings reconcile exactly. The payroll liability balance is $38,400 below the payroll-supported amount.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":4,"prompt":"How would you trace quarter-end adjustment and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Trace the $38,400 liability reduction to a manual quarter-end adjustment by the Payroll Manager. Review FB03 document and approval references; no second approval is on file. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B46-PY-04-ManualAdjustment-FB03.pdf","options":["Trace the $38,400 liability reduction to a manual quarter-end adjustment by the Payroll Manager. Review FB03 document and approval references; no second approval is on file.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":5,"prompt":"How would you conclude and recommend and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Request the manager''s rationale and prior-quarter adjustment review. Recommend mandatory second approval for manual payroll GL adjustments above a low materiality threshold, including at period end. Evidence: THORNFIELD-B46-PY-04-ManualAdjustment-FB03.pdf","options":["Request the manager''s rationale and prior-quarter adjustment review. Recommend mandatory second approval for manual payroll GL adjustments above a low materiality threshold, including at period end.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0}]'::jsonb);
insert into tib_sweep_private.bank(chapter,questions) values (47,'[{"id":1,"prompt":"How would you engagement scoping and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Obtain fictitious Thornfield S4Q system inventory, finance process map and quarterly control register. Confirm scope exclusions with sponsor. Evidence: Signed scope, population inventory and control owner matrix","options":["Obtain fictitious Thornfield S4Q system inventory, finance process map and quarterly control register. Confirm scope exclusions with sponsor.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":2,"prompt":"How would you test strategy and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Define population, period, sample basis, tolerable deviation and evidence attributes. Document reliance on automated controls separately. Evidence: Approved test script and sampling rationale","options":["Define population, period, sample basis, tolerable deviation and evidence attributes. Document reliance on automated controls separately.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":3,"prompt":"How would you evidence collection and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Obtain approved exports with parameters, user IDs, timestamps and system identifiers. Verify totals and reconcile sample back to source. Evidence: Evidence register, exports and reconciliation","options":["Obtain approved exports with parameters, user IDs, timestamps and system identifiers. Verify totals and reconcile sample back to source.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":4,"prompt":"How would you remediation and retest and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Client introduces dual approval for sensitive bank changes. Test configuration and a new transaction; retain before/after and residual-risk evidence. Evidence: Retest script, evidence and owner sign-off","options":["Client introduces dual approval for sensitive bank changes. Test configuration and a new transaction; retain before/after and residual-risk evidence.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0},{"id":5,"prompt":"How would you management reporting and support your conclusion?","anchor":"Prepare executive summary with scope, exceptions, severity rationale, owner, due date, remediation status and limitations. Escalate overdue actions. Evidence: Final report, exception tracker and sponsor decision","options":["Prepare executive summary with scope, exceptions, severity rationale, owner, due date, remediation status and limitations. Escalate overdue actions.","Accept management''s explanation without reconciling it to source evidence.","Use only records already reported as successful or approved.","Conclude the control is effective before validating population, timing and exceptions."],"answer":0}]'::jsonb);

select set_config('request.jwt.claim.sub',(select user_id::text from public.enrollments where course='TIB-FULL-SWEEP' and is_active and (start_date is null or start_date<=current_date) and (expiry_date is null or expiry_date>=current_date) limit 1),true) is not null as fixture_ready;
set local role authenticated;
do $$ declare r jsonb;begin
r:=public.tib_sweep_assessment('state',0,'{}');if r->>'mode'<>'guided' then raise exception 'Default mode failed';end if;
begin perform public.tib_sweep_assessment('submit',2,'{"answers":[0,0,0,0,0]}');raise exception 'Predecessor lock failed';exception when insufficient_privilege then null;end;
r:=public.tib_sweep_assessment('submit',1,'{"answers":[0,0,1,1,1]}');if (r->>'passedAttempt')::boolean then raise exception '40 percent passed';end if;
r:=public.tib_sweep_assessment('submit',1,'{"answers":[0,0,0,1,1]}');if (r->>'score')::numeric<>60 or not (r->>'passedAttempt')::boolean then raise exception '60 percent failed';end if;
r:=public.tib_sweep_assessment('submit',1,'{"answers":[1,1,1,1,1]}');if not r->'passed' @> '[1]'::jsonb then raise exception 'Retained pass lost';end if;
perform public.tib_sweep_assessment('mode',0,'{"mode":"self-study"}');r:=public.tib_sweep_assessment('submit',47,'{"answers":[1,1,1,1,1]}');if r->'passed' @> '[47]'::jsonb then raise exception 'Opt-out falsely passed';end if;
perform public.tib_sweep_assessment('mode',0,'{"mode":"guided"}');begin perform public.tib_sweep_assessment('submit',47,'{"answers":[0,0,0,0,0]}');raise exception 'Restored gate failed';exception when insufficient_privilege then null;end;
if has_table_privilege('authenticated','tib_sweep_private.progress','INSERT') or has_table_privilege('authenticated','tib_sweep_private.bank','SELECT') or has_function_privilege('anon','public.tib_sweep_assessment(text,integer,jsonb)','EXECUTE') then raise exception 'ACL failed';end if;
end $$;
select 'PASS Full Sweep exact 60%, failure, retained passes, predecessor gates, opt-out/return and ACLs under authenticated role' as result;
rollback;